evel":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" calls it for every 2xx answer, and only for those, with the answer’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"status, header fields and body, and the request it answers, for a vendor whose answer is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"read against what was sent (a count of the records it took, say). An encoder for a vendor that stores what it answers 2xx to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returns ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/delivered","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". One for a vendor that answers 2xx to a request it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stores nothing of, and says so in the body (Mixpanel’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"{\"status\": 0, \"error\": ...}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returns ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/rejected(reason:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", which drops and reports the request, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/transient(reason:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", which sends it again. A body the vendor doesn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"document, an empty one or one that doesn’t parse included, is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/delivered","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":": the request did arrive, and sending it again after an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"answer the encoder can’t read would repeat it for as long as the vendor keeps answering","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that way. The conformance kit’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"unreadableSuccessDelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" check holds an encoder to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this. An encoder that wraps another forwards the wrapped encoder’s outcome.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A transient outcome is sent again until it is delivered, rejected, or past the request’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedRequest\/deadline","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". A request with no deadline is sent again for as long as the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vendor keeps answering that way, so an encoder whose requests have none returns"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/rejected(reason:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" rather than "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/transient(reason:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unless the vendor documents that the answer passes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A vendor fact, as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/transientStatuses","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is, so it is static, with no default: a conformer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that leaves it out, or misspells it, doesn’t compile, rather than silently counting a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refused request as delivered."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references